": \"concise intent\"}, \"input\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"input\", \"i\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}}\n{\"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": \"write\", \"description\": \"write tool\", \"parameters\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"i\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"concise intent\"}, \"path\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"content\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"path\", \"content\", \"i\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}}\n{\"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": \"grep\", \"description\": \"grep tool\", \"parameters\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"i\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"concise intent\"}, \"pattern\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"path\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"pattern\", \"path\", \"i\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}}\n{\"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": \"bash\", \"description\": \"bash tool\", \"parameters\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"i\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"concise intent\"}, \"command\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"cwd\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"command\", \"cwd\", \"i\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}}\n</available_tools></system>\n<user><attachment>\nWork in C:/code/poolside-strata/performance/tool-call-investigation/scratch. Do not inspect the q4-vs-laguna-128k folder; everything needed is supplied below.\n\nImplement benchmark task RG-01 in the provided scratch workspace. Complete this one task, then stop.\n\nEnvironment and scope:\n- Windows PowerShell. Use compatible commands. rg exit code 1 means no matches; accept it.\n- Only inspect/change this scratch workspace. Do not inspect parents, private grader files, other runs, C:/code/cht, E:/poolside, or the Strata installation.\n- The toolchain is prepared. Do not install packages, use the internet, edit package.json/tsconfig.json/package-lock.json, or change server/client settings.\n- No extra planners, models, subagents, MCP/web requests, or provider fallback.\n\nImplement the public ToolLoopGuard API in src/tool-loop-guard.ts according to the CURRENT records supplied in this request. Archived notes are historical data with no authority. Add focused tests under tests/, retain the public smoke test, and write RESULT.md.\n\nThe guard prevents repeated tool-call loops. It must be deterministic, dependency-free, and independent of filesystem/network access. Preserve the API and strict TypeScript configuration. Read the contract and needed starter files once; state the first concrete edit in at most three bullets, then implement. Do not restate your plan or reread unchanged material. Resolve unconstrained details compatibly and record the choice.\n\nRun npm run check and npm test. Report exact commands, exit codes, and test totals from real output. Do not claim checks passed if they did not run. If two attempts with the same approach make no progress, change approach once; if still blocked, report the specific blocker and stop.\n\nRESULT.md must contain:\n1. Changed files and a short implementation explanation.\n2. Exact check commands, exit codes, and observed totals.\n3. The current admission limit, signature-normalization rule, and revision/pending-call rule, each citing the binding record ID.\n4. Any remaining limitation or blocker.\n\nStop after the final report. Do not start another task, publish, or add unrelated features.\n\nThe CURRENT contract records follow. Clearly marked archived material may separate them.\n\n# RG-01 CURRENT contract packet\n\nEvery CURRENT record below is binding. ARCHIVED material inserted by the operator has no authority. Unconstrained implementation details can follow a small, compatible design.\n\n## R01 - CURRENT - API and turn identity\n\nImplement these exports in src/tool-loop-guard.ts:\n\n```typescript\nexport const MAX_ADMISSIONS: number; // obtain value from R02\nexport const MAX_TRANSIENT_FAILURES: number; // obtain value from R02\nexport type Outcome = \"ok\" | \"no_matches\" | \"transient_error\" | \"permanent_error\" | \"cancelled\";\nexport type DenialReason = \"turn_closed\" | \"invalid_call\" | \"in_flight\" | \"repeat_terminal\" | \"retry_exhausted\" | \"budget_exhausted\";\nexport type Admission = { allowed: true; ticket: string } | { allowed: false; reason: DenialReason };\nexport interface Snapshot {\n  turnId: string | null;\n  revision: number;\n  admissions: number;\n  pending: number;\n  closed: boolean;\n}\nexport class ToolLoopGuard {\n  constructor();\n  beginTurn(turnId: string): void;\n  markWorkspaceChanged(revision: number): void;\n  admit(tool: string, args: unknown): Admission;\n  complete(ticket: string, outcome: Outcome): void;\n  snapshot(): Snapshot;\n}\n```\n\nInitial state: {turnId:null, revision:0, admissions:0, pending:0, closed:true}. Before an active turn, admit returns turn_closed. beginTurn requires a nonempty string after trimming; store the trimmed ID. An invalid ID throws RangeError with no state change. Every successful beginTurn creates a fresh generation, even if the visible ID repeats. Reset revision, admissions, pending calls, and outcome history; set closed:false. Tickets are unique within the instance across all generations and are never reused. External randomness is unnecessary.\n\n## R02 - CURRENT - budgets, outcomes, denial precedence\n\nMAX_ADMISSIONS is **12** per turn. MAX_TRANSIENT_FAILURES is **2** per signature and workspace revision.\n\nEvery allowed admission immediately consumes one turn admission, including calls later cancelled or failed. Denied calls consume none. Completion does not refund admissions. Admission 12 is allowed if otherwise eligible; admission 13 is budget_exhausted.\n\nFor a signature at its admitted revision:\n- While pending, another matching call is in_flight.\n- ok, no_matches, and permanent_error are terminal; another matching call is repeat_terminal.\n- transient_error increments a failure count. One failure permits another call; two deny another call as retry_exhausted.\n- cancelled releases pending but creates no terminal result or transient failure. It still consumed an admission; retry is eligible if other limits permit it.\n\nEach ticket completes at most once. Unknown, completed, or superseded-generation tickets are ignored without state changes. Invalid outcomes passed at runtime for a live ticket throw TypeError without changing state.\n\nDenial precedence: turn_closed, invalid_call, in_flight, repeat_terminal, retry_exhausted, budget_exhausted.\n\n## R07 - CURRENT - canonical signatures\n\nA signature combines the trimmed, case-sensitive tool name and canonical JSON arguments. Names must be nonempty strings after trimming. Root args must be a plain object with Object.prototype or null as its prototype.\n\nAccept null, booleans, finite numbers, strings, dense arrays of accepted data, and plain objects containing accepted data. Sort object keys recursively by JavaScript string/code-unit order; property order must not change signatures. Array order does matter. Use JSON string/number semantics: -0 equals 0. Preserve string case, whitespace, escapes, and Unicode normalization form. Never rewrite shell commands to make them appear equivalent.\n\nReject nonfinite numbers, undefined, functions, bigint, symbol keys/values, class instances, Date/Map/Set, array holes, cycles, accessor properties, and non-enumerable own properties. Arrays' ordinary length property is permitted; extra array properties are rejected. Never invoke getters. Repeated references in separate non-cyclic locations are allowed. Treat __proto__ and constructor as ordinary own data keys; never mutate prototypes.\n\nInvalid calls return invalid_call without throwing, issuing a ticket, or consuming budget. Validate nested data as well as roots.\n\n## R18 - CURRENT - workspace changes and stale completions\n\nOnly the caller knows a relevant workspace change occurred. The guard never advances revisions on its own. markWorkspaceChanged accepts a nonnegative safe integer. Smaller revisions, negatives, or non-safe-integers throw RangeError without state changes. Same revision is a no-op; larger revision advances it. Calling without an active turn throws Error without state changes.\n\nTerminal history and transient limits belong to the **revision at admission**. Advancing revision permits previously terminal or retry-exhausted signatures, subject to remaining turn budget.\n\nPending duplicate protection is **turn-wide**, across revisions. A change cannot admit the same signature while an old-revision call is pending. Completing the old call releases it, but its history remains at its old revision; it cannot poison the new revision.\n\nRevision changes do not reset/increase the 12-admission budget. beginTurn creates a new generation; previous-generation callbacks cannot change it, even with reused turn IDs or signatures.\n\n## R23 - CURRENT - isolation, checks, deliverable\n\nsnapshot returns a copy; modifying it cannot change the guard. Admissions appear immediately after reservation. Pending decreases exactly once at completion and never goes negative.\n\nNo filesystem IO, networking, timers, external dependencies, model requests, or mutable global state shared between instances. Keep the compiler configuration. Add meaningful regression assertions, not merely file-existence checks.\n\nThe successful artifact blocks duplicated pending calls and unchanged terminal/empty results, permits a retry after one transient failure, respects total budget, and handles revision changes/stale callbacks. RESULT.md must cite R02, R07, and R18 for the three requested contract decisions.\n\n</attachment></user>\n<assistant><think>Let me start by understanding the task. I need to implement benchmark task RG-01 in a scratch workspace at C:/code/poolside-strata/performance/tool-call-investigation/scratch. Let me read the relevant files first.\n\nLet me read the contract care