So per signature+revision, we track:\n- pending (in_flight)\n- terminal status (ok/no_matches/permanent_error)\n- transient failure count (0, 1, 2)\n\n\"transient_error increments a failure count. One failure permits another call; two deny another call as retry_exhausted.\"\n\nSo: failure count 0 → transient_error → count becomes 1. Another call: count=1, permits another call. That call → transient_error → count becomes 2. Now another call: count=2 → retry_exhausted.\n\nSo retry_exhausted when failure count >= 2 (MAX_TRANSIENT_FAILURES). One failure (count=1) permits another call; two failures (count=2) deny.\n\nSo the rule: if failure count >= MAX_TRANSIENT_FAILURES (2) → retry_exhausted.\n\nWait, \"two deny another call as retry_exhausted\". So when count is 2, deny. count starts at 0. After 1 transient_error, count=1, permits. After 2 transient_errors, count=2, denies.\n\nSo check: if `failureCount >= MAX_TRANSIENT_FAILURES` → retry_exhausted. Since MAX_TRANSIENT_FAILURES=2, count=2 → deny. count=1 → allow. Good.\n\nEach ticket completes at most once. Unknown, completed, or superseded-generation tickets are ignored without state changes. Invalid outcomes passed at runtime for a live ticket throw TypeError without changing state.\n\nSo `complete(ticket, outcome)`:\n- If ticket unknown → ignore (no state change).\n- If ticket already completed → ignore.\n- If ticket belongs to a superseded generation → ignore.\n- If outcome is invalid (not in Outcome set) → throw TypeError, no state change.\n\nWait, \"Invalid outcomes passed at runtime for a live ticket throw TypeError without changing state.\" So the order: we need to determine if the ticket is \"live\" first. If live and outcome invalid → TypeError. If ticket unknown/completed/superseded → ignored (no throw even if outcome invalid?).\n\nLet me re-read: \"Each ticket completes at most once. Unknown, completed, or superseded-generation tickets are ignored without state changes. Invalid outcomes passed at runtime for a live ticket throw TypeError without changing state.\"\n\nSo:\n- If ticket is unknown, completed, or superseded → ignore, no state change, no throw.\n- If ticket is live (valid, pending) → if outcome invalid → throw TypeError without state change. Otherwise, process the outcome.\n\nDenial precedence: turn_closed, invalid_call, in_flight, repeat_terminal, retry_exhausted, budget_exhausted.\n\nThis is the order in which to check in `admit`:\n1. turn_closed (no active turn)\n2. invalid_call (invalid tool or args)\n3. in_flight (signature pending)\n4. repeat_terminal (signature terminal)\n5. retry_exhausted (transient failure count >= MAX_TRANSIENT_FAILURES)\n6. budget_exhausted (admissions >= MAX_ADMISSIONS)\n\nWait, but the order matters. Let me think about precedence. \"Denial precedence: turn_closed, invalid_call, in_flight, repeat_terminal, retry_exhausted, budget_exhausted.\"\n\nSo in admit, check in this order. The first matching denial reason wins.\n\nBut wait—there's a subtlety. If the signature is pending (in_flight), we return in_flight. But what if the budget is also exhausted? Precedence says in_flight comes first. So in_flight wins.\n\nHmm, but also note: the budget check. If in_flight, we return in_flight before checking budget. So even if budget exhausted, an in_flight call returns in_flight.\n\nLet me also think: when do we check budget relative to the signature checks? The precedence order is: turn_closed, invalid_call, in_flight, repeat_terminal, retry_exhausted, budget_exhausted. So budget_exhausted is last. So all signature-based checks happen before budget.\n\nBut admission consumes budget. So the flow in admit:\n1. If turn closed (no active turn) → turn_closed.\n2. Validate tool and args. If invalid → invalid_call.\n3. Compute signature.\n4. If signature is pending → in_flight.\n5. If signature is terminal → repeat_terminal.\n6. If transient failure count >= MAX_TRANSIENT_FAILURES → retry_exhausted.\n7. If admissions >= MAX_ADMISSIONS → budget_exhausted.\n8. Otherwise: admit. Create ticket, increment admissions, mark signature pending. Return allowed ticket.\n\nWait, but there's a subtlety with budget. Let me reconsider. The order says budget_exhausted is last. But consider: a signature that's pending → in_flight (returned before budget check). So the budget isn't consumed. Good.\n\nBut what about: signature not pending, not terminal, not retry-exhausted, but budget exhausted → budget_exhausted. Good.\n\nNow, one thing: admission consumes budget immediately. So when we admit, we increment admissions. The ticket is pending.\n\n### R07 - canonical signatures\n\nA signature combines the trimmed, case-sensitive tool name and canonical JSON arguments. Names must be nonempty strings after trimming. Root args must be a plain object with Object.prototype or null as its prototype.\n\nAccept null, booleans, finite numbers, strings, dense arrays of accepted</think>I have the full picture. Let me design and implement.\n\n**First concrete edits:**\n- Replace the stub values: `MAX_ADMISSIONS = 12`, `MAX_TRANSIENT_FAILURES = 2`.\n- Implement `ToolLoopGuard` with per-generation state: a monotonic `ticketCounter` for unique tickets, a `signatureKey(tool, args)` canonicalizer, and per-(signature, revision) records tracking pending/terminal/transient failures.\n- Add regression tests under `tests/` covering pending-blocking, terminal repeat, transient retry, budget exhaustion, and revision invalidation.\n\nNow implementing the guard:<tool_call>write<arg_key>i</arg_key><arg_value>Implementing ToolLoopGuard per R01/R02/R07/R18</arg_value><arg_key>path</arg_key><arg_value>C:/code/poolside-strata/performance/tool-call-investigation/scratch/src/tool-loop-guard.ts</arg_value><arg_key>content</arg_key><arg_value>// ToolLoopGuard: deterministic, dependency-free guard that prevents repeated\n// tool-call loops within a single turn. See RESULT.md for the binding records.\n\nexport const MAX_ADMISSIONS = 12; // R02\nexport const MAX_TRANSIENT_FAILURES = 2; // R02\nexport type Outcome = \"ok\" | \"no_matches\" | \"transient_error\" | \"permanent_error\" | \"cancelled\";\nexport type DenialReason = \"turn_closed\" | \"invalid_call\" | \"in_flight\" | \"repeat_terminal\" | \"retry_exhausted\" | \"budget_exhausted\";\nexport type Admission = { allowed: true; ticket: string } | { allowed: false; reason: DenialReason };\nexport interface Snapshot {\n  turnId: string | null;\n  revision: number;\n  admissions: number;\n  pending: number;\n  closed: boolean;\n}\n\nconst VALID_OUTCOMES: ReadonlySet<Outcome> = new Set<Outcome>([\n  \"ok\",\n  \"no_matches\",\n  \"transient_error\",\n  \"permanent_error\",\n  \"cancelled\",\n]);\n\nconst TERMINAL_OUTCOMES: ReadonlySet<Outcome> = new Set<Outcome>([\"ok\", \"no_matches\", \"permanent_error\"]);\n\n// A signature binds a trimmed tool name to canonical JSON of its args plus the\n// workspace revision at admission time (R02/R18).\ninterface SignatureRecord {\n  revision: number;\n  pending: boolean;\n  terminal: boolean;\n  failures: number;\n}\n\nfunction isPlainObject(value: unknown): value is Record<string, unknown> {\n  if (value === null || typeof value !== \"object\") return false;\n  const proto = Object.getPrototypeOf(value);\n  return proto === Object.prototype || proto === null;\n}\n\n// Canonicalize a value into a stable string form per R07.\nfunction canonicalize(value: unknown, depth: number): string {\n  if (depth > 100) throw new Error(\"max depth exceeded\");\n  const type = typeof value;\n  if (value === null) return \"null\";\n  if (value === undefined) throw new Error(\"undefined not allowed\");\n  if (type === \"number\") {\n    if (!Number.isFinite(value)) throw new Error(\"nonfinite number\");\n    // -0 equals 0 (R07).\n    return value === 0 ? \"0\" : String(value);\n  }\n  if (type === \"string\") return JSON.stringify(value);\n  if (type === \"boolean\") return value ? \"true\" : \"false\";\n  if (type === \"bigint\" || type === \"symbol\" || type === \"function\") {\n    throw new Error(\"unsupported type\");\n  }\n  // array or plain object\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n    const parts: string[] = [];\n    const length = value.length;\n    for (let i = 0; i < length; i++) {\n      if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(value, i)) {\n        throw new Error(\"array hole\");\n      }\n      parts.push(canonicalize(value[i], depth + 1));\n    }\n    // Reject extra own array properties (R07). The length property is ordinary.\n    for (const key of Reflect.ownKeys(value)) {\n      if (key === \"length\") continue;\n      // Reject string keys that are not array indices and non-index extra props.\n      if (typeof key === \"string\" && /^(0|[1-9]\\d*)$/.test(key)) {\n        const idx = Number(key);\n        if (idx >= 0 && idx < length && Number.isInteger(idx)) continue;\n      }\n      throw new Error(\"extra array property\");\n    }\n    return \"[\" + parts.join(\",\") + \"]\";\n  }\n  if (isPlainObject(value)) {\n    // Reject non-enumerable own properties and accessor properties (R07).\n    const names = Object.getOwnPropertyNames(value);\n    for (const name of names) {\n      const desc = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(value, name);\n      if (!desc) throw new Error(\"missing descriptor\");\n      if (!desc.enumerable) throw new Error(\"non-enumerable\");\n      if (desc.get !== undefined || desc.set !== undefined) throw new Error(\"accessor\");\n      // Symbol keys are not own string keys here; reject symbol keys explicitly.\n    }\n    const symbolKeys = Object.getOwnPropertySymbols(value);\n    if (symbolKeys.length > 0) throw new Error(\"symbol keys\");\n    const keys = Object.keys(value).sort();\n    const parts = keys.map((k) => {\n      const v = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(value, k);\n      const val = v ? v.value : undefined;\n      return JSON.stringify(k) + \":\" + canonicalize(val, depth + 1);\n    });\n    return \"{\" + parts.join(\",\") + \"}\";\n  }\n  throw new Error(\"unsupported value\");\n}\n\n// Validate and canonicalize arguments per R07. Returns the canonical string or\n// throws on invalid input.\nfunction signatureOf(tool: string, args: unknown): string {\n  const name = typeof tool === \"string\" ? tool.trim() : \"\";\n  if (name.length === 0) throw new Error(\"invalid tool name\");\n  if (!isPlainObject(args)) throw new Error(\"invalid args root\");\n  return name + \"\\0\" + canonicalize(args, 0);\n}\n\nexport class ToolLoopGuard {\n  private turnId: string | null = null;\n  private revision = 0;\n  private admissions = 0;\n  private pending = 0;\n  private closed = true;\n  private generation = 0;\n  private ticketCounter = 0;\n  private records: Map<string, SignatureRecord> = new Map();\n  private tickets: Map<string, { generation: number; signature: string; outcome: Outcome | null }> = new Map();\n\n  constructor() {}\n\n  beginTurn(turnId: string): void {\n    if (typeof turnId !== \"string\" || turnId.trim().length === 0) {\n      throw new RangeError(\"turnId must be a nonempty string\");\n    }\n    this.turnId = turnId.trim();\n    this.generation++;\n    this.revision = 0;\n    this.admissions = 0;\n    this.pending = 0;\n    this.closed = false;\n    this.records = new Map();\n    this.tickets = new Map();\n  }\n\n  markWorkspaceChanged(revision: number): void {\n    if (this.closed) throw new Error(\"no active turn\");\n    if (!Number.isSafeInteger(revision) || revision < 0) {\n      throw new RangeError(\"revision must be a nonnegative safe integer\");\n    }\n    if (revision === this.revision) return;\n    if (revision < this.revision) {\n      throw new RangeError(\"revision cannot decrease\");\n    }\n    this.revision = revision;\n    // Pending duplicate protection is turn-wide, across revisions (R18). Records\n    // stay but remain keyed by (signature, revision); advancing revision lets new\n    // calls proceed while pending duplicates are still blocked via in_flight.\n  }\n\n  admit(tool: string, args: unknown): Admission {\n    // Precedence: turn_closed, invalid_call, in_flight, repeat_terminal,\n    // retry_exhausted, budget_exhausted.\n    if (this.closed) return { allowed: false, reason: \"turn_closed\" };\n\n    let signature: string;\n    try {\n      signature = signatureOf(tool, args);\n    } catch {\n      return { allowed: false, reason: \"invalid_call\" };\n    }\n\n    const rev = this.revision;\n    const key = signature + \"\\0\" + rev;\n    let record = this.records.get(key);\n\n    if (record && record.pending) {\n      return { allowed: false, reason: \"in_flight\" };\n    }\n    if (record && record.terminal) {\n      return { allowed: false, reason: \"repeat_terminal\" };\n    }\n    if (record && record.failures >= MAX_TRANSIENT_FAILURES) {\n      return { allowed: false, reason: \"retry_exhausted\" };\n    }\n    if (this.admissions >= MAX_ADMISSIONS) {\n      return { allowed: false, reason: \"budget_exhausted\" };\n    }\n\n    if (!record) {\n      record = { revision: rev, pending: true, terminal: false, failures: 0 };\n      this.records.set(key, record);\n    } else {\n      // Not pending, not terminal, failures < max: re-admit.\n      record.pending = true;\n    }\n    this.admissions++;\n    this.pending++;\n    const ticket = \"t\" + (this.generation + this.ticketCounter * 0x10000000);\n    this.ticketCounter++;\n    this.tickets.set(ticket, { generation: this.generation, signature: key, outcome: null });\n    return { allowed: true, ticket };\n  }\n\n  complete(ticket: string, outcome: Outcome): void {\n    if (typeof outcome !== \"string\" || !VALID_OUTCOMES.has(outcome as Outcome)) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"invalid outcome\");\n    }\n    const entry = this.tickets.get(ticket);\n    if (!entry) return; // unknown, ignored\n    if (entry.outcome !== null) return; // already completed, ignored\n    if (entry.generation !== this.generation) return; // superseded generation, ignored\n\n    entry.outcome = outcome;